t="_blank">Web of Science</a></div><div class="core-xlink-google-scholar"><a href="https://scholar.google.com/scholar_lookup?title=The+mortality+burden+of+untreated+aortic+stenosis.&amp;publication_year=2023&amp;journal=J+Am+Coll+Cardiol&amp;pages=2101-2109&amp;doi=10.1016%2Fj.jacc.2023.09.796&amp;pmid=37877909" target="_blank">Google Scholar</a></div><div class="to-citation__accordion no-separator" id="core-collateral-to-citation__accordion-r2" role="menu" aria-label="Citations links" style="display: none;"><ul role="none"><li role="none"><a class="to-citation" href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa2405880#core-r1-1" target="_self" role="menuitem"><i class="icon-return" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>a [...] than 3% of adults 65 years of age or older. </span></a></li><li role="none"><a class="to-citation" href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa2405880#core-r2-2" target="_self" role="menuitem"><i class="icon-return" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>b [...] in which aortic stenosis is undertreated. </span></a></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div><div class="biblioentry" data-has="label"><div class="label">3.</div><div id="core-collateral-r3" class="citations"><div class="citation"><div class="citation-content">Otto CM, Nishimura RA, Bonow RO, et al. 2020 ACC/AHA guideline for the management of patients with valvular heart disease: a report of the American College of Cardiology/American Heart Association Joint Committee on Clinical Practice Guidelines. <em>J Am Coll Cardiol</em> 2021;77(4):e25-e197.</div><div class="external-links"><div class="to-citation__wrapper"><button class="to-citation__toggle" aria-controls="core-collateral-to-citation__accordion-r3" data-trigger="dropdown" aria-label="Toggle citations menu"><i class="icon-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="accordion__toggle__title" data-expand-title="Hide Citations" data-collapsed-title="Show Citations"></span></button></div><div class="core-xlink-crossref"><a href="https://doi.org/1